  "id": "COMPOUND:26074 - PROTEIN:4915",
  "verbalization": "Epi-Fibrauretinoside A is implicated in the inhibition of Replicase polyprotein 1ab through a multi-step mechanism involving dual serine/threonine and tyrosine protein kinases. This pathway is targeted by multiple compounds, including Javanicoside F, Ascidiathiazone B, and Corticatic Acid E, all of which share a common target in the same kinase. The evidence suggests that Epi-Fibrauretinoside A may act through a similar mechanism, potentially modulating the kinase activity that is essential for the replication of the replicase polyprotein. The consistent targeting of this kinase by different compounds supports the hypothesis that Epi-Fibrauretinoside A may exert its effect by influencing the same biological process, thereby contributing to the inhibition of Replicase polyprotein 1ab. The presence of multiple independent pathways converging on this kinase indicates a plausible and robust mechanism, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the exact nature of the interaction.",
